            <div xml:id="d433">

                <pb facs="0511" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg407"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4342: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-20T18:00:00+08:00">February 20, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 20—1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>90. Your telegram No. 10, February 10, 11 a.m. My reply to Mayor’s letters of
                    February 8th regarding responsibility of each side for damages was sent February
                    13th and British reply February 15th.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>At consular body meeting February 17th French Consul General proposed that
                        in addition to individual replies Senior Consul should send a reply on
                        behalf of consular body. This was acquiesced in and a reply was sent by me
                        as Senior Consul February 18th.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Following is text of letter dated February 20th sent by Senior Consul to
                        Japanese Consul General regarding landing of Japanese forces in Settlement:
                            <quote rend="blockquote">
                            <p>“With regard to the disembarkation of Japanese naval and military
                                forces which has taken place in the International Settlement, I have
                                the honor at the desire of my interested colleagues to protest
                                against the use by those forces of the International Settlement as a
                                base or channel of military operations unconnected with the defense
                                of the Settlement.[”]</p></quote></item>
                </list>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation and Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
